cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or these data, please cite both the article and this archive."
title: "volta-drought-propagation: code and derived data for sparse-gauge tests of drought propagation in the Volta Basin"
abstract: >-
  Code and derived data for a study of hydrological drought propagation in the Volta Basin above
  Akosombo (18 GRDC gauges, 1961-2007; GPCC rainfall 1951-2020; 16 CMIP6 models). The scripts
  (i) test for change points and trends in rainfall, drought synchrony and runoff at fixed
  rainfall; (ii) relate basin drought to six climate indices with wavelet coherence, seasonal
  correlations and event-rate models; (iii) match daily SSI drought events between linked gauges
  with observation-conditioned measures, an availability-aware permutation null, equivalence
  tests against the Ebro Basin, identifiability and synthetic-truth experiments and a GEOGLOWS v2
  reanalysis network; and (iv) drive a leakage-free hybrid wavelet-machine learning transfer
  model with bias-adjusted CMIP6 output to project drought risk and the monitoring horizon needed
  to test propagation. GRDC daily discharge is not redistributed.
